WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:04.291
A till app is what your staff use at the counter.

00:00:04.291 --> 00:00:08.419
This video follows one day at the till, step by step, and shows

00:00:08.419 --> 00:00:11.830
what each step leaves for the manager in the admin:

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:15.420
the shift, the sales, the cash drawer and the returns.

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:25.113
The till is an app that signs staff in and sells through the commerce API.

00:00:25.113 --> 00:00:30.460
The same products, prices, coupons, gift cards and stock as your online store.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.799
No till app ships in this solution.

00:00:33.799 --> 00:00:38.599
Your developers, or a partner, build one, or adapt one, using the API.

00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:43.020
What the site gives is the registers, the shifts, and the rules.

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:48.394
Every shift, sale and cash movement says who made it, because staff sign

00:00:48.394 --> 00:00:50.350
in with their own accounts.

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:55.169
One.

00:00:55.169 --> 00:00:59.691
Staff pick a register and open a shift, counting the opening float:

00:00:59.691 --> 00:01:02.230
the cash that starts in the drawer.

00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:03.562
Two.

00:01:03.562 --> 00:01:05.073
They ring up a sale:

00:01:05.073 --> 00:01:09.609
scan or search for products, change quantities, add a discount code or a

00:01:09.609 --> 00:01:13.040
gift card, and choose the customer, if they want one.

00:01:13.790 --> 00:01:14.540
Three.

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.290
They take the payment:

00:01:16.290 --> 00:01:21.229
cash, with change given, a card on the counter terminal with its approval

00:01:21.229 --> 00:01:25.230
code, a card on a Stripe reader, a gift card or a balance,

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:26.730
or a mix of these.

00:01:27.480 --> 00:01:28.226
Four.

00:01:28.226 --> 00:01:32.093
The receipt is printed, or emailed to the customer.

00:01:32.093 --> 00:01:32.839
Five.

00:01:32.839 --> 00:01:35.145
Cash is put in or taken out:

00:01:35.145 --> 00:01:38.740
change, banking at noon, and a reason for each.

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:40.148
Six.

00:01:40.148 --> 00:01:42.518
Returns are taken at the till:

00:01:42.518 --> 00:01:46.599
choose the sale, the items, and how the money goes back.

00:01:46.599 --> 00:01:47.389
Seven.

00:01:47.389 --> 00:01:51.470
At closing, staff count the drawer, and close the shift.

00:01:55.676 --> 00:01:59.828
In the admin, Commerce, Registers lists your registers:

00:01:59.828 --> 00:02:04.456
each with its store address, whether it is on, and its shifts.

00:02:04.909 --> 00:02:08.909
Under Shifts, the shift open at the till right now is listed.

00:02:08.909 --> 00:02:09.745
Open it:

00:02:09.745 --> 00:02:14.163
it shows the sales so far, the opening float the shift started with,

00:02:14.163 --> 00:02:17.029
and the cash that should be in the drawer.

00:02:21.218 --> 00:02:23.549
A closed shift shows its sales:

00:02:23.549 --> 00:02:27.769
how many, the total, the cash kept, what was paid by card, by

00:02:27.769 --> 00:02:30.918
gift card or balance, and what was refunded.

00:02:31.371 --> 00:02:32.903
And its cash drawer.

00:02:32.903 --> 00:02:37.087
The opening float, plus the cash put in, less what was taken out,

00:02:37.087 --> 00:02:40.151
gives the cash that should be there, Expected.

00:02:40.151 --> 00:02:43.628
What staff counted is next to it, and the Difference.

00:02:43.628 --> 00:02:48.991
Each cash movement is listed with who made it, and why, and the shift's closing note.

00:02:53.197 --> 00:02:57.324
Every register sale is a paid order, marked with its register.

00:02:57.324 --> 00:03:02.059
It appears in Commerce, Orders like any other order, with its lines, tax

00:03:02.059 --> 00:03:05.337
and payments, and the customer if there was one.

00:03:05.787 --> 00:03:09.600
A return at the till shows as a refund on the order, in

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:13.100
the same shift, so the drawer and the books agree.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:19.037
Under Orders, a sale that was returned is marked Refunded, and its page shows the refund.

00:03:22.837 --> 00:03:24.721
A shop with a counter:

00:03:24.721 --> 00:03:28.017
online and in-store sales, one stock count.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.356
A market stall:

00:03:30.356 --> 00:03:33.307
a tablet, cash and a card reader.

00:03:34.057 --> 00:03:35.584
Several stores:

00:03:35.584 --> 00:03:39.217
a register for each, and one set of reports.

00:03:41.217 --> 00:03:45.817
With registers and shifts, a day at the till adds up, to the cent.

00:03:45.817 --> 00:03:47.477
Thanks for watching.

